-- ccc23-review-boards.l4 -- sections 672.38 to 672.43 (Review Boards) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. Section 672.44 (rule-making and regulation-making powers) is machinery and has no function here (NOTES.md, coverage: inert, reason 2).
-- This is the part of the Code that says what a Review Board must look like for its decision to be "the decision of a Review Board".

§ `Section 672.38 -- Review Boards to be established`

-- 672.38(1): a Review Board shall be established or designated for each province to make or review dispositions concerning any accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible or unfit to stand trial is rendered,
-- and shall consist of not fewer than five members appointed by the lieutenant governor in council of the province.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13506 | 672.38 (1) A Review Board shall be established or designated for each province to make or review dispositions concerning any accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible by reason of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered, and shall consist of not fewer than five members appointed by the lieutenant governor in council of the province.
@ref s 672.38(1) (src:13506)
GIVEN `the number of members` IS A NUMBER
      `the members are appointed by the lieutenant governor in council of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.38(1) the Review Board is constituted as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the number of members` AT LEAST 5 AND `the members are appointed by the lieutenant governor in council of the province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall consist of not fewer than five members appointed by the lieutenant governor in council of the province"

-- 672.38(2): a Review Board shall be treated as having been established under the laws of the province.
-- src:13508 | (2) A Review Board shall be treated as having been established under the laws of the province.
@ref s 672.38(2) (src:13508)
GIVEN `it is a Review Board established or designated for a province under subsection 672.38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.38(2) the Review Board is treated as having been established under the laws of the province` MEANS
    IF `it is a Review Board established or designated for a province under subsection 672.38(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A Review Board shall be treated as having been established under the laws of the province"

-- 672.38(3): no member of a Review Board is personally liable for any act done in good faith in the exercise of the member's powers or the performance of the member's duties and functions, or for any default or neglect in good faith in the exercise of those powers or the performance of those duties and functions.
-- Asked in the positive (is the member personally liable?): the text says no for an act, default or neglect in good faith; it is silent otherwise.
-- src:13510 | (3) No member of a Review Board is personally liable for any act done in good faith in the exercise of the member’s powers or the performance of the member’s duties and functions or for any default or neglect in good faith in the exercise of those powers or the performance of those duties and functions.
@ref s 672.38(3) (src:13510)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act, default or neglect was in good faith in the exercise of the member’s powers or the performance of the member’s duties and functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.38(3) the member of a Review Board is personally liable` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of a Review Board` AND `the act, default or neglect was in good faith in the exercise of the member’s powers or the performance of the member’s duties and functions`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No member of a Review Board is personally liable for any act done in good faith"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say when a member is liable

§ `Sections 672.39 to 672.42 -- Members, chairperson, quorum, vote`

-- 672.39: a Review Board must have at least one member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry and, where only one member is so entitled, at least one other member must have training and experience in the field of mental health,
-- and be entitled under the laws of a province to practise medicine or psychology.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13512 | 672.39 A Review Board must have at least one member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry and, where only one member is so entitled, at least one other member must have training and experience in the field of mental health, and be entitled under the laws of a province to practise medicine or psychology.
@ref s 672.39 (src:13512)
GIVEN `the number of members entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry` IS A NUMBER
      `at least one other member has training and experience in the field of mental health and is entitled under the laws of a province to practise medicine or psychology` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.39 the Review Board has the members the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of members entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the number of members entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry` EQUALS 1 AND `at least one other member has training and experience in the field of mental health and is entitled under the laws of a province to practise medicine or psychology` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Review Board must have at least one member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry"

-- 672.4(2): where the chairperson of a Review Board established before the coming into force of subsection (1) is not a judge or other person referred to in it, the chairperson may continue to act until the expiration of the term of office
-- if at least one other member is a judge or other person referred to in subsection (1) or is a member of the bar of the province. A transitional rule, encoded because it bears on whether a chairperson may act.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13516 | (2) Where the chairperson of a Review Board that was established before the coming into force of subsection (1) is not a judge or other person referred to therein, the chairperson may continue to act until the expiration of his or her term of office if at least one other member of the Review Board is a judge or other person referred to in subsection (1) or is a member of the bar of the province.
@ref s 672.4(2) (src:13516)
GIVEN `the Review Board was established before the coming into force of subsection 672.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chairperson is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of office has not expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one other member of the Review Board is a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1) or is a member of the bar of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.4(2) the chairperson may continue to act until the expiration of the term of office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Review Board was established before the coming into force of subsection 672.4(1)` AND `the chairperson is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the chairperson of a Review Board that was established before the coming into force of subsection (1) is not a judge or other person referred to therein"
        IF `the term of office has not expired` AND `at least one other member of the Review Board is a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1) or is a member of the bar of the province` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if at least one other member of the Review Board is a judge or other person referred to in subsection (1) or is a member of the bar of the province"

-- 672.4(1): subject to subsection (2), the chairperson of a Review Board shall be a judge of the Federal Court or of a superior, district or county court of a province, or a person who is qualified for appointment to, or has retired from, such a judicial office.
-- fork: F-SUBJECT
-- src:13514 | 672.4 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the chairperson of a Review Board shall be a judge of the Federal Court or of a superior, district or county court of a province, or a person who is qualified for appointment to, or has retired from, such a judicial office.
@ref s 672.4(1) (src:13514)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of the Federal Court or of a superior, district or county court of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is qualified for appointment to such a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has retired from such a judicial office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chairperson may continue to act under subsection 672.4(2), by s 672.4(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.4(1) the person may be the chairperson of a Review Board` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the chairperson may continue to act under subsection 672.4(2), by s 672.4(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF `the person is a judge of the Federal Court or of a superior, district or county court of a province` OR `the person is qualified for appointment to such a judicial office` OR `the person has retired from such a judicial office` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the chairperson of a Review Board shall be a judge of the Federal Court or of a superior, district or county court of a province, or a person who is qualified for appointment to, or has retired from, such a judicial office"

-- 672.41(2): where the chairperson of a Review Board that was established before the coming into force of this section is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1), the quorum is constituted by the chairperson,
-- a member who is entitled to practise psychiatry, and a member who is a person referred to in that subsection or a member of the bar of the province.
-- src:13520 | (2) Where the chairperson of a Review Board that was established before the coming into force of this section is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1), the quorum of the Review Board is constituted by the chairperson, a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry, and a member who is a person referred to in that subsection or a member of the bar of the province.
@ref s 672.41(2) (src:13520)
GIVEN `the Review Board was established before the coming into force of section 672.41 and its chairperson is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member who is a person referred to in subsection 672.4(1) or a member of the bar of the province is present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.41(2) the quorum of the Review Board is constituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Review Board was established before the coming into force of section 672.41 and its chairperson is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the chairperson of a Review Board that was established before the coming into force of this section is not a judge or other person referred to in subsection 672.4(1)"
        IF `the chairperson is present` AND `a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry is present` AND `a member who is a person referred to in subsection 672.4(1) or a member of the bar of the province is present` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the quorum of the Review Board is constituted by the chairperson, a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry, and a member who is a person referred to in that subsection or a member of the bar of the province"

-- 672.41(1): subject to subsection (2), the quorum of a Review Board is constituted by the chairperson, a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry, and any other member.
-- fork: F-SUBJECT
-- src:13518 | 672.41 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the quorum of a Review Board is constituted by the chairperson, a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry, and any other member.
@ref s 672.41(1) (src:13518)
GIVEN `the chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other member is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 672.41(2) applies, by s 672.41(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.41(1) the quorum of the Review Board is constituted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection 672.41(2) applies, by s 672.41(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF `the chairperson is present` AND `a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry is present` AND `any other member is present` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the quorum of a Review Board is constituted by the chairperson, a member who is entitled under the laws of a province to practise psychiatry, and any other member"

-- 672.42: a decision of a majority of the members present and voting is the decision of a Review Board.
-- src:13522 | 672.42 A decision of a majority of the members present and voting is the decision of a Review Board.
@ref s 672.42 (src:13522)
GIVEN `the number of members present and voting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who vote for the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.42 the decision is the decision of the Review Board` MEANS
    IF `the number of those members who vote for the decision` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the number of members present and voting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A decision of a majority of the members present and voting is the decision of a Review Board"

§ `Section 672.43 -- Powers of Review Boards`

-- 672.43: at a hearing held by a Review Board to make a disposition or review a disposition in respect of an accused, the chairperson has all the powers that are conferred by sections 4 and 5 of the Inquiries Act on persons appointed as commissioners under Part I of that Act.
-- The Inquiries Act is not among the sources: the function says that the chairperson has those powers, not what they are.
-- src:13524 | 672.43 At a hearing held by a Review Board to make a disposition or review a disposition in respect of an accused, the chairperson has all the powers that are conferred by sections 4 and 5 of the Inquiries Act on persons appointed as commissioners under Part I of that Act.
@ref s 672.43 (src:13524)
GIVEN `it is a hearing held by a Review Board to make a disposition or review a disposition in respect of an accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.43 the chairperson has the powers conferred by sections 4 and 5 of the Inquiries Act on commissioners` MEANS
    IF `it is a hearing held by a Review Board to make a disposition or review a disposition in respect of an accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a hearing held by a Review Board to make a disposition or review a disposition in respect of an accused"
